The key takeaway is that service communication is not just choosing between REST and Kafka. It is the combination of protocol, communication style, service discovery, data format, contract compatibility, reliability, security, and observability. A strong microservices engineer understands how these pieces interact and can justify the trade-offs for a particular business workflow.
